WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.610
A bigger context window looks like free capacity.

00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:04.748
It is not.

00:00:04.848 --> 00:00:06.870
So what does the model really see?

00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:11.937
In Lost in the Middle, the answer's position changed the score.

00:00:11.987 --> 00:00:17.965
First document, seventy-five point eight percent. Middle, fifty-three point eight.

00:00:18.015 --> 00:00:23.940
End, sixty-three point two. With no documents at all, fifty-six point one.

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:27.718
Buried in the middle, the model did worse than with nothing.

00:00:28.268 --> 00:00:30.814
Caching pays for stillness.

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:34.896
Cache reads cost a tenth of the base rate, ten times cheaper.

00:00:34.946 --> 00:00:39.578
But a timestamp in the system prompt guarantees a miss on every call.

00:00:40.128 --> 00:00:46.164
Every piece of context belongs in exactly one of four places. The system prompt,

00:00:46.214 --> 00:00:49.470
the tools, the disk, and the tail.

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:53.399
The session is the workbench for one conversation.

00:00:53.449 --> 00:00:57.181
Memory is the filing cabinet that persists across them.

00:00:57.231 --> 00:01:00.322
Extracted facts, not raw dialogue.

00:01:00.872 --> 00:01:04.550
And in practice, a subagent is a context firewall.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:11.226
That's module one, context. Start with page one: How models read context.
